That's a known paradoxical stimulant response and it's actually diagnostic.

In neurotypical brains caffeine increases alertness. In ADHD brains the stimulant hits the dopamine system differently — you get the peripheral effects (jitters) but also a calming or even sedating effect on the central nervous system. The euphoria is your dopamine-starved brain getting an unexpected hit. Then the crash.

